---

This repository contains a patch that makes a third-party client borrow the
official opencode client's TLS identity in order to pass a client-identity
check on opencode.ai's free tier. That check may exist precisely to keep
third-party clients out, and bypassing it may violate the upstream service's
terms of use. By using this software you accept that you are responsible for
complying with those terms and for any consequence of not doing so. The
authors make no representation about, and take no responsibility for, the
upstream service's availability, policies, or the outcome of using this patch.

This repository does not contain upstream source code. The upstream project
(dsh-our-free-model, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ebony-Vinyl) is referenced only by
a diff against its public 2.8.0 release.
